EDM4hep MCParticle times are in ns, but Delphes expects the time component of Candidate::Position in mm/c (the standalone readers pass Pythia's tProd() in mm/c, and DelphesRootReader converts seconds to mm/c). The framework input conversion passed the ns value directly, so in k4SimDelphesAlg all production times seen by Delphes were too small by a factor c

Effects in the framework (k4run) case, measured against the standalone DelphesPythia8_EDM4HEP with the same generator events:
- times of the re-exported Particle collection were 1/c of the correct value;
- the track time at the vertex (TrackerHits hit 0) was 1/c of the standalone value for all non-prompt tracks;
- times at the calorimeter (track TOuter, calorimeter hits) lacked the production time of displaced particles;
